<h1>Job Attributes Summary</h1>

<p>The attributes summary page shows solver results aggregated by result
attributes (e.g., sat, unsat, unknown) for all solver/configuration pairs
in a given job space.
</p>

<h2>Attributes Table</h2>
<p>Each row represents a solver/configuration pair. The columns show the
distinct result attribute values found across all benchmarks. Each cell
displays <strong>"count / time"</strong>, where count is the number of
benchmarks that produced that attribute and time is the total wallclock
(or CPU) time for those benchmarks.
</p>

<h2>Totals Table</h2>
<p>The totals table aggregates counts and times across all solvers for each
attribute value, giving an overview of the entire job space.
</p>

<h2>Switching Time Metric</h2>
<p>Click the <strong>"use CPU time"</strong> button to toggle between wallclock
time and CPU time in the time columns. Click again to switch back to wallclock
time.
</p>

<h2>Space Navigation</h2>
<p>Use the space tree on the left to navigate to sub-spaces within the job.
Clicking a sub-space reloads the page with that space's attribute summary.
</p>
